        "answer": {
          "short": "The area multiplies by $4$.",
          "worked": "The original area is $A=\\pi r^{2}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A_{\\text{new}}&=\\pi(2r)^{2}\\\\A_{\\text{new}}&=4\\pi r^{2}\\\\A_{\\text{new}}&=4A\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe area multiplies by $4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
